# Form & Validation Standards

## Input Variant

Always use `variant="filled"` for all MUI TextField, Select, and Autocomplete inputs.
Never mix `outlined` and `filled` in the same form.

## Required Fields

- Mark required fields with `*` in the label: `label="First name *"`
- Use `required` prop on the MUI TextField for HTML validation
- Show a form-level note: "Fields marked * are required" at the top of the form when there are 3+ required fields

## Validation Approach

- Run validation on blur (`onBlur`) for field-level errors — not only on submit
- Run full validation on submit
- Error messages must be specific and human-readable:
  - ✅ "Employee code must be 2–32 lowercase letters, numbers, or hyphens"
  - ❌ "Invalid format"
  - ✅ "Joining date cannot be in the future"
  - ❌ "Invalid date"
- Use `helperText` on MUI TextField to show errors — never use `alert()` or `window.confirm()`

## Field Groups

Use the `FormSection` component to group related fields visually:
- Personal information group
- Contact details group
- Role & department group
- Dates group

Example groups for staff creation:
- Personal: First Name, Last Name, Date of Birth
- Employment: Employee Code, Designation, Department, Joining Date, Role
- Contact: Email, Phone

## Autofill Handling

All forms must handle browser autofill gracefully:
- The MUI theme overrides `-webkit-autofill` so filled fields don't turn dark blue
- Test login form with browser saved credentials — should look consistent

## Success & Error Feedback

- After successful create/update/delete: show MUI Snackbar (bottom-left, auto-dismiss after 4s) with green success message
- After API error: show MUI Alert `severity="error"` above the form with the error message
- Never silently succeed or fail — always give feedback

## Confirmation Dialogs

- Destructive actions (delete, deactivate, retire, close) must show a MUI Dialog confirmation:
  - Title: "Confirm [action]"
  - Body: Specific impact text — "This will permanently deactivate [Name]. They will no longer be able to log in."
  - Actions: "Cancel" (left) and "[Action]" in `color="error"` (right)
- Do NOT use browser `confirm()` dialog

## Loading States in Forms

- Submit button shows a CircularProgress spinner and is disabled while the API call is in progress
- Form fields should be disabled (or read-only) during submission to prevent double-submit
- Use `isSubmitting` state to control this

## Form Page Layout

- Max-width for forms: 720px on desktop (don't stretch to full width)
- Two-column layout for simple field pairs (Name + Code, Start Date + End Date) on `md+`
- Single column on mobile
- Submit / Cancel buttons: right-aligned at the bottom of the form section
